WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.140
Shirahata Kiichiro!

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.900
He's a diplomat who once worked 
for the ambassador to Britain.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.690
We suspect this Shirahata has learned the 
specifics of high command's "Grand Strategy."

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.570
I can confirm Graham is "black."

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.410
Kill without hesitation.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.740
Die with honor.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:22.570
You're now officially a part of "Wind Agency."

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.330
"We can't use War College grads."

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.290
The words of D-Agency's founder, Yuuki.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.630
Yuuki...

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.760
I'm told you connected
Shirahata to Graham.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.460
Can you secure the location 
of the exchange?

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:45.230
Yes. I've already planted an 
operative inside Shirahata's villa.

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.230
Once you successfully 
complete this operation,

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.970
your "Wind Agency" will be

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:54.860
officially recognized as the 
Imperial Army's espionage agency.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.800
D-Agency has also been informed 
of the Shirahata situation.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.720
I have no intention of 
playing a double-joker game.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.140
Whichever one of you fails 
will be considered the spare.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.660
This mission will decide everything.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.680
Whether or not my Wind Agency can

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.700
get the better of D-Agency...

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:28.410
The ones to survive

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.270
will be us.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.570
<i>As the embers of world war smoldered</i>

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.030
<i>in autumn of 1937,</i>

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.950
<i>the Imperial Army</i>

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:39.950
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.700
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:43.220
<i>established a clandestine 
spy training agency.</i>

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.840
<i>The histories, names, and even ages</i>

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.620
<i>of the elite men who pass its 
rigorous application process</i>

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.890
<i>are all treated as top-secret information.</i>

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:58.300
<i>They easily complete training 
exercises that push them</i>

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.190
<i>to their physical and mental limits.</i>

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.600
<i>Under the command of founder 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki,</i>

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:06.350
<i>they operate worldwide, within the shadows.</i>

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.650
<i>And so a brand-new intelligence 
agency was created.</i>

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.850
<i>Its name is "D-Agency."</i>

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:48.910
Long ago, we'd cross the 
ridge riding in a palanquin...

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:53.920
Episode 8 - Double Joker (Part 2)

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:54.400
Now I lie dreaming, riding steam trains...

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.400
Take this to the Mist Room.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.460
The smoke turns the tunnel black as pitch...

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:55.570
Yes.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.260
My, oh my, black as pitch...

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:06.640
Oh!

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.620
Sir, your room is the next one down the hall.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.560
Oh... I'm terribly sorry for the interruption.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.520
No, no, don't worry about it.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:23.530
This program is a work of fiction. 
The characters, organizations, locations, laws, names, 
etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.680
Who was that?

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.210
The man using the next room over.

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.290
He said he works for a company
in Tokyo and is training here.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.000
Anyway, how about it?

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.000
Sir?

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.280
I'm still plenty young, you know.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.890
Oh, dear. Cut that out!

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.890
So then I said...

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:00.230
<b>Mist</b>

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:01.740
Really?

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:05.390
Huxley-san is at home relaxing.

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:06.360
Huxley (Shirahata)

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:09.010
I'm told the flower arrangement was delivered.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.160
Flower Arrangement (Morishima)

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:16.900
Care for some more?

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:20.870
Thanks. Thanks.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.210
The customer just left.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.760
Customer (Graham)

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.640
So far, so good, then.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.310
Excuse me. I apologize for 
interrupting your meal.

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:36.100
Another person from your party is here.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:37.780
He said...

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:40.780
you'd know who he was 
without hearing his name...

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.180
He said he's here to see the manager...

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:45.780
Send him in.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.420
You can go and rest now.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.440
You needn't wake me up tomorrow morning.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:07.180
As you wish, sir.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:10.790
Oh, did you contact Churchill?

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:13.860
Yes, just before Morishima-san left.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:17.180
Ah, he must've gone to the inn to see

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.890
that waitress again.

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.900
I envy how close they are.

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.050
Goodnight.

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:05.790
U-Um... Where is this?

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:08.190
What do you want from me?

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:11.240
Morishima Kunio.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:15.660
A student living in Shirahata's villa since last year, serving as his houseboy.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.200
Born in Tokyo, 1918.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.410
Formerly named Ikeda Kunio.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:25.140
After the Morishima family adopted you, 
they paid off an army doctor,

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:28.090
and you were sent home
immediately after your physical exam.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:31.560
Draft-dodging with falsified medical 
records gets you three years.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:32.550
No...

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:37.010
If you're drafted and sent to the front lines, 
you'll likely only live a few months.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:40.200
P-Please overlook this!

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:42.720
It was all my parents' doing!

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:49.550
We suspect Shirahata is a spy.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:51.770
See where I'm going?

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:56.040
Here's your chance to prove 
your loyalty to Japan.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:01.340
Well? Anything strange happening at the villa?

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.740
He usually leaves the dog out at night,

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:06.640
but tonight he wanted him put in the shed.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:10.790
Also, he said there was no need 
to make breakfast tomorrow.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.470
And the thing we discussed?

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:17.300
The desk in the study.

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:18.930
I see!

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:23.930
You've done excellent work.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.820
So... As for that other matter...

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.360
Are you going to let me off the hook?

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:30.830
Of course!

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:34.010
You've more than met our expectations.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:35.110
I thank you.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:48.250
Hey. Someone call a car to take him home.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:49.570
I'll do it.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:51.270
Oh, no need!

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:52.670
I can get home by myself.

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:55.040
There's no need for that.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.430
I won't see you much after this,

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:00.320
and they might be getting 
worried about you back home.

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:19.700
Get me a new sake cup.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.810
Kill without hesitation.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:39.180
Die with honor.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.170
O-Oh...

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:45.140
Are you all right?

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.830
Yes... Just a bit tipsy...

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:49.900
I don't usually drink.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.860
Is something wrong?

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:53.560
Oh, no, no.

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:55.870
He just drank a little too much, that's all.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.960
Let's get going.

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:05.950
Listen up, men.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:08.810
Our training excursion ends today.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.790
You've all done well.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.450
One final task remains,

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:15.540
and then we're done.

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:18.640
I expect to see your training pay off.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:22.930
The exchange happens at 0300, as planned.

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:26.350
We'll be on our way, then.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:29.940
Take care not to bother Huxley-san.

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:33.460
<i>Yuuki...</i>

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:36.750
<i>I hope to see you show up in person, if I can.</i>

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.110
<i>And when you do...</i>

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:41.710
There's our customer.

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:42.340
Sir.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:43.890
Status?

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:45.180
In position.

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:48.610
<i>Yuuki...</i>

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:51.780
<i>He couldn't nail down the location, huh?</i>

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:53.190
<i>Fool.</i>

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:57.360
Come on.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.000
Sir.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:29.770
We wait here until 0300.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:30.500
Sir.

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:33.380
Detain anyone who shows up.

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:36.210
If they even try to resist, kill them.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.610
What the hell...

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.750
Why isn't anyone here?

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:04.380
You're late.

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:14.790
Yuuki!

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:21.120
You bastard, how'd you—

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:22.460
How did I?

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:25.650
I drove in through the front gate.

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:28.720
You tipped off Graham and Shirahata!

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:31.880
Don't tell me the Grand Strategy's...

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:33.940
Grand Strategy?

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:38.280
Nothing like that was here to begin with.

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:42.390
Well, even after reading it,

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:45.340
it was really just absolute nonsense.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.250
Absolute nonsense?

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:50.780
It's the Imperial Army's greatest secret!

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:55.020
It contains high command's 
most fundamental strategies!

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:56.710
In the end,

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:59.420
it's nothing more than general theories

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.490
and principles related to strategy.

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:05.610
What good does it do to
treat that as some kind of

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.490
legendary treatise on the military arts?

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:13.160
In other words, it shows the limits 
of Army War College graduates.

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:17.410
You're an Army Lieutenant 
Colonel yourself, and you—

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:32.970
Yuuki.

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:37.860
Know what the biggest difference is between 
your D-Agency and my Wind Agency?

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:43.080
Your motto is, "Don't die. Don't kill."

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:46.900
But we believe in killing when necessary.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.880
It's true you beat us to the punch,

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:55.760
but the Grand Strategy is definitely here.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:15:00.160
And we'll get it, even if it 
means killing Shirahata.

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:03.420
That's how Wind Agency operates.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:07.550
I win, Yuuki.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:21.060
Oh, boy.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:30.890
Son of a...

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:36.240
We had such great bait, and all we 
caught were shrimps like you guys.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.740
You're... from D-Agency?!

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:41.650
The fake history and draft-dodging

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:43.790
was a half-hidden cover story.

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:46.790
You know, a type of security alarm.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.760
If another spy agency tried to get to Shirahata,

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:52.750
they'd go after Morishima without question.

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:55.300
But you...

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:57.590
were Shirahata's houseboy

00:15:57.590 --> 00:16:00.660
for over a year...

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:05.310
Morishima...

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:07.910
Impossible! How are you on your feet?

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:09.980
I had the same tool as you.

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:12.100
I just used it the opposite way.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:20.650
Kaminaga and Hatano have detained

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:24.170
everyone hidden around the villa's grounds.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:29.840
Shirahata informed Graham 
of the army's movements.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:33.040
Graham feared being arrested, 
and left with his wife

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:35.720
to catch a boat to Shanghai.

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:36.920
What?!

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:38.840
We've had our eye

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:44.190
on Shirahata since long before 
your group started to act.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:45.440
He's one of

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:49.360
the very few channels 
to England we have left.

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.100
If we keep him under tight surveillance,

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:54.050
he's still plenty useful to us.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:57.950
Don't you lay a finger on 
Shirahata over a trifle like this.

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:01.960
Though even if you did try to arrest him,

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:04.200
you've got no evidence.

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:08.240
<i>No evidence?!</i>

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:13.880
<i>That's because you disposed of it all!</i>

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.640
Yuuki!

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:26.980
Killing is the worst decision a spy can make.

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:30.960
All it does is spur outside investigations.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:34.320
It's a meaningless, foolish act.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:38.700
In other words, proof you're 
not qualified to be a spy.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.740
Your reasons don't matter.

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:45.910
It doesn't change the fact that 
you leaked our plan to Shirahata!

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.110
I hope you're ready to be court-martialed!

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:50.460
Unfortunately,

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:54.380
we're not the ones who told Shirahata.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:18:01.310
Do you remember the waitress who 
served you at the inn tonight?

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.950
How do you know about her?

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:11.150
Were you staying at the same inn as us?

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:13.950
Oh, you didn't notice?

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:15.940
We ran into each other once.

00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:28.510
Excuse me.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:33.500
The customer leaving just now 
was a bit unsteady on his feet.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:38.180
Yes, he's a student earning his keep 
working as a houseboy for Shirahata-san.

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:40.970
Apparently he's not used to alcohol.

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:44.960
That was quite

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:47.770
the doting look you had on your face.

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:55.670
Though if he returns to the villa in that state, 
he'll probably be scolded, poor thing.

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:02.940
I-I'll go and phone Shirahata-san's villa.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:05.540
I'll tell them he was 
goaded into drinking a lot.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:07.960
Yes, good idea.

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:16.670
Shirahata figured out the situation 
from the waitress's call,

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:18.470
and quickly fled.

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:20.580
That's all.

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:26.000
Attempting to court-martial

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:28.430
will only humiliate you further.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:31.220
And I'll tell you one more thing.

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:34.480
All the women at that inn were fully aware

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:37.290
of your true identities as military men.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:39.190
What do you mean?!

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:41.710
The ground war is intensifying,

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:45.260
and young men are constantly
being called to battle.

00:19:46.390 --> 00:19:48.080
There's been a huge decline

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.590
in groups of young men staying at the inn.

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:53.490
Students would be suspect enough,

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:58.810
but a group of seven or eight young businessmen?

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:00.670
Anyone would notice.

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:07.140
Do you know the meaning of 
the War College emblem?

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:10.210
It's the currency of the Edo period,

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:11.890
worth eight rin.

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:15.450
"It's so large, yet not even worth one sen."

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:18.020
That means in the real world, it's worthless.

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:20.860
But for some reason,

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:23.130
for those affiliated with the army,

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:25.040
it carries the opposite meaning.

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:30.000
That's why even a lowly inn 
waitress saw through you.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:34.770
You're all emperors with no clothes,

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:37.630
running around playing spy.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:24.340
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:24.340
An English expedition has gone to Egypt.

00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:28.630
You need to be prepared for 
consequences if you go tomb-raiding.

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:33.140
Sometimes the mummy hunter 
ends up becoming the mummy.

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:34.880
Episode 10 - Pursuit
